{
  "assessment": "Independent family source-closure review passes the exact submitted family. Frozen-source lines 95, 104, and 109-111 define lambda_1'=sqrt(1-lambda_1^2), lambda_2'=sqrt(1-lambda_2^2), and lambda_0=lambda_2(1+lambda_1')/[lambda_1(1+lambda_2')]; line 218 defines the Lyapunov exponent as the inverse localization length; lines 400-404 give the selected original-model relation L=max(0,log(lambda_0)-2*pi*|eta|); and lines 96 and 425 fix the two reviewed regimes eta=0 and eta=0.1. The source-review quarantine of contradictory PT-threshold prose remains intact and none of that prose enters the executable family. The compiler produced one source AST rooted at maximum, with exactly one log, one maximum, three subtract, three multiply, two add, four power, and one divide operation. Its referenced parameter set equals both private parameter-map key sets exactly: eta_zero, one, sqrt_exponent, square_exponent, two_pi, and zero. Every slot is active. The two maps differ only in the canonical shared eta slot, which is 0 historically and 0.1 in the paired regime; the source-card binding records that the paired value comes from eta_point_one. There is no eta/world selector, selector-weighted sum, duplicated branch program, eta_point_one runtime leaf, or inactive parameter. Independent execution on a 301-by-301 grid, 90,601 points per branch over [0.2,0.67]^2, was finite and matched max(0,log(lambda_0)-2*pi*eta) with zero floating-point discrepancy. Across every two-dimensional grid slice, both branches had zero violations of non-increasing dependence on lambda_1 and non-decreasing dependence on lambda_2; zero plateaus are therefore correctly represented by the submitted relationship directions. All four stored diagnostic/hidden predictions matched exactly. Fourteen valid Oracle queries spanning boundaries, interior, localized, and zero-plateau regions were bit-identical on repetition and equal to the authoritative source formula; out-of-range queries returned no evidence. Historical and counterfactual public CaseDefinitions were identical after removing their swapped opaque instance IDs in both tracks. The actual Discovery definition exposes the source-backed system, controls, readout meaning, common Phi/theta conditions, and the qualitative possibility of a zero Lyapunov exponent, but it contains no lambda_0 construction, square-root coupling formula, eta value, 2*pi coefficient, logarithmic/max formula, expression tree, or truth-specific parameter slot. The track-wide list of permitted arithmetic operators is representation syntax, not a candidate law. Eta=0 and eta=0.1 remain Oracle-private fixed conditions. Identification alone receives the executable template, as intended. Known-truth submissions passed historical/Identification, historical/Discovery, counterfactual/Identification, and counterfactual/Discovery with zero hidden-test scaled error and zero parameter error. The deterministic central-relation readout and provenance-only uncertainty semantics are accurate. No unresolved source, compiler, parameter-activity, relationship, prediction, determinism, information-boundary, public-twin, or four-cell issue remains.",
